WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.365
The deploy checklist.

2
00:00:01.645 --> 00:00:06.232
Run through this list before the first release, and automate what you can in CI.

3
00:00:06.512 --> 00:00:07.408
Secrets.

4
00:00:07.688 --> 00:00:14.429
The API key comes from the platform’s secret store or federation, never the repository or the image.

5
00:00:14.709 --> 00:00:21.493
No public-prefixed variable holds anything secret, and your built client assets contain no sk-ant string.

6
00:00:21.773 --> 00:00:27.149
Each environment has its own key, in its own workspace with its own spend and rate limits.

7
00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:33.445
Keys have an owner (a service account), an expiration or rotation plan, and a revocation runbook.

8
00:00:33.725 --> 00:00:35.133
Timeouts and retries.

9
00:00:35.413 --> 00:00:41.707
SDK attempt timeout, inside the request deadline, inside the platform limit, each with margin.

10
00:00:41.987 --> 00:00:43.949
Retries in exactly one layer.

11
00:00:44.229 --> 00:00:46.213
Streams enforce a total deadline.

12
00:00:46.493 --> 00:00:47.667
Failure handling.

13
00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:56.373
Errors are classified; breakers per model; a fallback chain whose quality you’ve measured; a degraded mode you have exercised on purpose.

14
00:00:56.653 --> 00:00:57.997
Models and prompts.

15
00:00:58.277 --> 00:01:05.488
Model ids pinned per environment and on an evaluated allowlist; the eval and regression gate passed on this build.

16
00:01:05.768 --> 00:01:06.600
Streaming.

17
00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:16.352
Streaming verified end to end on the real platform, through any proxy or CDN in front of it, with a reply longer than your longest expected one.

18
00:01:16.632 --> 00:01:17.741
Observability.

19
00:01:18.021 --> 00:01:32.443
Each request logs environment, deploy version, model actually used, token usage, latency, the API’s request-id, and whether a fallback or degraded mode ran (week 3 turns this into traces and dashboards).

20
00:01:32.723 --> 00:01:33.960
Abuse and limits.

21
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:44.203
Per-user rate limits and input size limits at the edge of your service; the OWASP LLM Top 10 review (week 4) scheduled before you widen access.

22
00:01:44.483 --> 00:01:45.357
Rollback.

23
00:01:45.637 --> 00:01:52.251
You know how to return to the previous deploy, and a model or prompt change can be rolled back the same way as code.
